# Build output from the demo sources a chapter ships so its figures can be
# checked. Following the build line in optimizer-demo.rs drops a .s file next
# to it, and that should not show up as untracked work. This file is repository
# tooling configuration and keeps the Tock license, as learning/.lcignore does.
*.s

# Except one that is a source rather than build output. Chapter 6 ships the
# assembly its figures quote, and check.py assembles it on every run, so a
# clone without this file would run the gate green with the check silently
# skipped and the page citing a file that is not there. Which is what happened:
# the rule above was written for chapter 1's build artefact and swallowed
# chapter 6's source the first time it was committed. It then happened a second
# way: splitting chapter 1 renumbered that chapter to 7 and this negation kept
# naming 6, so the rule stopped matching. It survived only because the file was
# already tracked and `git check-ignore` reports a tracked file as not ignored
# -- the bug was invisible until the material was copied into a repository
# where it was not yet added.
!ch07-asking-the-kernel/syscall-demo.s

# The account-scoped links to the published copies of each chapter, which
# mkindex.py substitutes for relative paths when emitting the publishable
# cover. These are addresses on someone's account rather than part of a
# CC BY-SA work, so they stay out of a public branch; a clone still gets a
# cover whose links resolve, because the tracked index.html uses paths.
tools/artifact-urls.json
